The Cursor SDK, @cursor/sdk, is not bundled, not a dependency and not tested against: its licence is "SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE.md" and nothing from it is
copied here. src/families/cursor.mjs adapts ideas (error classes, the benign unhandled-rejection list, the resume no-progress rule, steer outcomes)
from T3 Code's packages/provider-cursor (same commit, MIT, same notice).

The read-only readers (src/families/cursorReaders.mjs and the usage/models parts of src/families/muse.mjs) adapt logic and response shapes from T3 Code
(same commit, MIT, same notice): packages/provider-cursor/src/server/{CursorSdkCatalog,usageLimits,apiKey}.ts and
packages/provider-muse/src/server/{modelCatalog,usageLimits}.ts, protocol.ts (MuseSubscriptionUsage). Their tests use synthetic data shaped like T3's
usageLimits.test.ts and modelCatalog.test.ts examples (no recorded transcript); nothing from the Cursor SDK is copied.

src/families/acp.mjs and src/families/acpAgents.mjs port, in plain JavaScript, the behaviour of T3 Code's ACP client and provider (same commit, MIT,
same notice): packages/effect-acp/src/{client,protocol,agent}.ts (JSON-RPC framing, initialize, session setup, prompt and cancel), and
packages/provider-acp/src/server/{AcpSessionRuntime,adapter,runtimeModel,sessionConfig,elicitationForm,stderr}.ts (session runtime, model and
config-option shaping, elicitation forms, stderr redaction) plus packages/provider-acp-registry/src/server/mcpTransport.ts for MCP transport
selection. No ACP SDK code is copied and no ACP package is added: the client is written here against the recorded wire.
